  (uuid_generate_v4(), 'signed-navajo-sterling-silver-storyteller-cuff-jerome-yazzie', '1616159099', 'https://www.etsy.com/listing/1616159099/signed-vintage-native-america-indian?click_key=EuJgNAiy871arif8sV1dFEH80b97%3ALTc643ca9b72b9cddd5eb27b5dc15d970420975137&click_sum=81c99247&ls=a&ga_order=most_relevant&ga_search_type=all&ga_view_type=gallery&ga_search_query=Navajo+jewelry&ref=search_grid-222806-12-10&sr_prefetch=1&pf_from=search&pro=1&frs=1&cns=1&sts=1',
   'Signed Navajo Sterling Silver Storyteller Cuff, Jerome Yazzie', 'SIGNED Authentic Vintage Beautiful Engraved Hand Stamped Navajo Sterling Silver Bracelet Cuff with Hogan and Horses Storyteller Cuff “Summer Camp” Many a summer was spent herding sheep Native American Navajo Sterling Silver Bracelet Cuff. Width of Cuff is a 3/8 inches. Length of Cuff is 7.25 inches including gap (6” + gap 1.25”= 7.25”) Stamped Sterling Hallmarked by Artist❤️Jerome Yazzie A Hogan is a traditional Navajo hut of logs and earth. For as long as anyone can remember, Churro sheep have been central to Navajo life and spirituality, yet the animal was nearly exterminated in modern times by outside forces who deemed it an inferior breed. Now, on a Navajo reservation of northern Arizona and New Mexico, the Churro is being shepherded back to health. The Navajo Nation is the size of West Virginia, and at last count, 175,000 people live here. Most people are spread out in small clusters that you see off in the distance from the highway. Amongst modern prefab houses and hogans, the multisided traditional homes of the Navajo, are often corrals with small bands of sheep grazing nearby.', 'turquoise-jewelry',
